# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two-qubit gate {#the-two-qubit-gate}"
msgstr "Ang two-qubit Gate {#the-two-qubit-gate}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every bond $(i, j)$ of the lattice gets the same two-qubit gate, made of a Heisenberg entangler followed by random fields:\n"
msgstr "Ang bawat bond $(i, j)$ ng lattice ay nakakakuha ng parehong two-qubit Gate, na binubuo ng Heisenberg entangler na sinusundan ng mga random na field:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"U_{ij} =  e^{iJ(X_iX_j + Y_iY_j + Z_iZ_j)}\\; e^{i(h_i Z_i + h_j Z_j)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"U_{ij} =  e^{iJ(X_iX_j + Y_iY_j + Z_iZ_j)}\\; e^{i(h_i Z_i + h_j Z_j)}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with $h$ drawn uniformly from $[-\\pi/2, \\pi/2]$ for every gate.\n"
msgstr "na may $h$ na iginuhit nang uniform mula sa $[-\\pi/2, \\pi/2]$ para sa bawat Gate.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "> **Question.** How would you decompose $U_{ij}$ into gates the hardware can run?\n"
msgstr "> **Question.** Paano mo hahatiin ang $U_{ij}$ sa mga Gate na kayang patakbuhin ng hardware?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Answer\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Sagot\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The fields** are easy. $e^{ihZ}$ is a single-qubit rotation $R_Z(-2h)$ on each qubit.\n"
msgstr "**Ang mga field** ay madali. Ang $e^{ihZ}$ ay isang single-qubit rotation na $R_Z(-2h)$ sa bawat Qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The entangler** is the hard part. $XX$, $YY$ and $ZZ$ commute, so it factors into three rotations, $R_{XX}$, $R_{YY}$ and $R_{ZZ}$. Each takes two CNOTs, which makes six CNOTs per gate.\n"
msgstr "**Ang entangler** ang mahirap na bahagi. Nagko-commute ang $XX$, $YY$ at $ZZ$, kaya nahahati ito sa tatlong rotation, $R_{XX}$, $R_{YY}$ at $R_{ZZ}$. Bawat isa ay nangangailangan ng dalawang CNOT, na nagiging anim na CNOT bawat Gate.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is a better way. Any two-qubit gate can be built from at most three CNOTs and single-qubit rotations. The optimal circuit starts from the form $e^{i(aXX + bYY + cZZ)}$, and this entangler already has that form with $a = b = c = J$. So it maps straight onto three CNOTs, and the single-qubit angles are linear in $J$. The experiment code builds the gate this way.\n"
msgstr "May mas magandang paraan. Ang anumang two-qubit Gate ay mabubuo mula sa hindi hihigit sa tatlong CNOT at mga single-qubit rotation. Nagsisimula ang optimal na Circuit sa anyong $e^{i(aXX + bYY + cZZ)}$, at ang entangler na ito ay may ganoong anyo na kapag $a = b = c = J$. Kaya direkta itong napupunta sa tatlong CNOT, at linear sa $J$ ang mga single-qubit angle. Ganito binubuo ng experiment code ang Gate.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "On hardware, every two-qubit gate adds noise, so halving the CNOT count matters.\n"
msgstr "Sa hardware, nagdaragdag ng noise ang bawat two-qubit Gate, kaya mahalaga ang paghahati sa kalahati ng bilang ng CNOT.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""

