# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulate the $4 \\times 4$ lattice {#simulate-the-4-times-4-lattice}"
msgstr "I-simulate ang $4 \\times 4$ na lattice {#simulate-the-4-times-4-lattice}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the $4 \\times 4$ lattice, you can do both: compute the exact state at every coupling, and sample every circuit with 10,000 shots, as an experiment would. The shots are stored with shape (batches, shots, qubits), the same layout as the randomizations in the hardware data. Here all 10,000 shots form a single batch, so the bootstrap over batches adds no shot noise, and the error bars in the next plot show only the spread between marginal positions.\n"
msgstr "Para sa $4 \\times 4$ na lattice, magagawa mo ang pareho: kalkulahin ang eksaktong state sa bawat coupling, at i-sample ang bawat Circuit gamit ang 10,000 shot, tulad ng gagawin ng isang experiment. Naka-store ang mga shot na may hugis (mga batch, mga shot, mga Qubit), ang parehong layout ng mga randomization sa data ng hardware. Dito, isang batch ang binubuo ng lahat ng 10,000 shot, kaya walang idinadagdag na shot noise ang bootstrap sa mga batch, at ang spread lang sa pagitan ng mga marginal na posisyon ang ipinapakita ng mga error bar sa susunod na plot.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. What to measure and how to estimate it {#2-what-to-measure-and-how-to-estimate-it}"
msgstr "2. Ano ang susukatin at paano ito tantiyahin {#2-what-to-measure-and-how-to-estimate-it}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The IPR and the collision entropy {#the-ipr-and-the-collision-entropy}"
msgstr "Ang IPR at ang collision entropy {#the-ipr-and-the-collision-entropy}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a marginal $A$ of $n_A$ qubits with bitstring distribution $p_A(a)$, the quantity to estimate is the inverse participation ratio (IPR) of the marginal distribution, and from it the collision entropy:\n"
msgstr "Para sa isang marginal na $A$ ng $n_A$ Qubit na may bitstring distribution na $p_A(a)$, ang dapat tantiyahin ay ang inverse participation ratio (IPR) ng marginal distribution, at mula rito ang collision entropy:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}_A = \\sum_a p_A(a)^2, \\qquad S_2[A] = -\\log_2 \\mathrm{IPR}_A\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}_A = \\sum_a p_A(a)^2, \\qquad S_2[A] = -\\log_2 \\mathrm{IPR}_A\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\mathrm{IPR}_A$ is also the probability that two shots agree on the marginal. A product state has $\\mathrm{IPR}_A = 1$, and a random state has $\\mathrm{IPR}_A \\approx 2^{-n_A}$, so $S_2$ climbs from 0 to about $n_A$ bits as the marginal becomes random.\n"
msgstr "Ang $\\mathrm{IPR}_A$ ay ang probabilidad din na magkasundo ang dalawang shot sa marginal. Ang product state ay may $\\mathrm{IPR}_A = 1$, at ang random state ay may $\\mathrm{IPR}_A \\approx 2^{-n_A}$, kaya umaakyat ang $S_2$ mula 0 hanggang halos $n_A$ bit habang nagiging random ang marginal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Estimator 1: count pairs of shots {#estimator-1-count-pairs-of-shots}"
msgstr "Estimator 1: bilangin ang mga pares ng shot {#estimator-1-count-pairs-of-shots}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "> **Question.** How do you estimate this quantity from your shots?\n"
msgstr "> **Question.** Paano mo tatantiyahin ang dami na ito mula sa iyong mga shot?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The naive estimator computes each $p(a)$ from the shots as $\\hat p(a) = n_a / N$, then sums $\\sum_a \\hat p(a)^2$.\n"
"This estimator is biased.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kinukwenta ng naive na estimator ang bawat $p(a)$ mula sa mga shot bilang $\\hat p(a) = n_a / N$, pagkatapos ay sinusuma ang $\\sum_a \\hat p(a)^2$.\n"
"Biased ang estimator na ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\sum_a n_a^2 / N^2$ counts every shot as agreeing with itself, which pushes the estimate up: on average it gives $\\mathrm{IPR}_A + (1 - \\mathrm{IPR}_A)/N$ instead of $\\mathrm{IPR}_A$. Since $\\mathrm{IPR}_A$ is the probability that two shots agree, count only pairs of *different* shots:\n"
msgstr "Binibilang ng $\\sum_a n_a^2 / N^2$ ang bawat shot bilang kasundo ang sarili nito, na nagtataas sa tantiya: sa karaniwan, ibinibigay nito ang $\\mathrm{IPR}_A + (1 - \\mathrm{IPR}_A)/N$ sa halip na $\\mathrm{IPR}_A$. Dahil ang $\\mathrm{IPR}_A$ ay ang probabilidad na magkasundo ang dalawang shot, bilangin lang ang mga pares ng *magkaibang* shot:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\widehat{\\mathrm{IPR}}_A = \\frac{\\sum_a n_a (n_a - 1)}{N (N - 1)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\widehat{\\mathrm{IPR}}_A = \\frac{\\sum_a n_a (n_a - 1)}{N (N - 1)}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is unbiased, and it is what `ipr_from_shots` below computes.\n"
msgstr "Unbiased ito, at ito ang kinukwenta ng `ipr_from_shots` sa ibaba.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Estimator 2: Parseval expansion {#estimator-2-parseval-expansion}"
msgstr "Estimator 2: Parseval expansion {#estimator-2-parseval-expansion}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The IPR can also be written through the parities $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ of all nonempty subsets $S$ of the marginal:\n"
msgstr "Maisusulat din ang IPR sa pamamagitan ng mga parity na $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ ng lahat ng hindi walang laman na subset na $S$ ng marginal:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}_A = 2^{-n_A}\\Bigl(1 + \\sum_{\\emptyset \\neq S \\subseteq A} \\langle Z_S \\rangle^2\\Bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}_A = 2^{-n_A}\\Bigl(1 + \\sum_{\\emptyset \\neq S \\subseteq A} \\langle Z_S \\rangle^2\\Bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This form matters because error mitigation methods such as PEA work on expectation values, not on probabilities.\n"
"**One qubit:** The outcome probabilities are $p(0) = (1 + \\langle Z \\rangle)/2$ and $p(1) = (1 - \\langle Z \\rangle)/2$, so\n"
msgstr ""
"Mahalaga ang anyong ito dahil gumagana ang mga paraan ng error mitigation tulad ng PEA sa mga expectation value, hindi sa mga probabilidad.\n"
"**Isang Qubit:** Ang mga probabilidad ng outcome ay $p(0) = (1 + \\langle Z \\rangle)/2$ at $p(1) = (1 - \\langle Z \\rangle)/2$, kaya\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR} = p(0)^2 + p(1)^2 = \\frac{1 + \\langle Z \\rangle^2}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
"**A $2 \\times 2$ marginal:** With its qubits labeled $a, b, c, d$, the marginal has $2^4 - 1 = 15$ parities: 4 single qubits, 6 pairs, 4 triples, and the whole marginal, so\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR} = p(0)^2 + p(1)^2 = \\frac{1 + \\langle Z \\rangle^2}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
"**Isang $2 \\times 2$ na marginal:** Kapag may label na $a, b, c, d$ ang mga Qubit nito, may $2^4 - 1 = 15$ parity ang marginal: 4 na single qubit, 6 na pares, 4 na triple, at ang buong marginal, kaya\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR} = \\frac{1}{16} \\Bigl(1\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_d \\rangle^2 \\\\\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a Z_b \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 \\\\\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a Z_b Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_b Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 \\\\\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a Z_b Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 \\Bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR} = \\frac{1}{16} \\Bigl(1\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_d \\rangle^2 \\\\\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a Z_b \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 \\\\\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a Z_b Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_b Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 \\\\\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a Z_b Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 \\Bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

