msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/onset-of-ergodicity/extracted-outputs/8680e8eb-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Brainstorm: how would you undo this? {#brainstorm-how-would-you-undo-this}"
msgstr "Brainstorm: paano mo ito aalisin? {#brainstorm-how-would-you-undo-this}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Suggested approach\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Iminumungkahing paraan\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At small $J$, the state is barely entangled, so the ideal answer there is cheap to compute classically, even for 64 qubits. That suggests measuring the effect of the noise at a small calibration coupling $J_0$ and correcting every other coupling with it. There are two natural ways to do that, called low-entanglement calibration (LEC):\n"
msgstr "Sa maliit na $J$, halos hindi entangled ang state, kaya madali sa classical na kalkulahin ang ideal na sagot doon, kahit para sa 64 qubit. Ibig sabihin, masusukat ang epekto ng noise sa isang maliit na calibration coupling na $J_0$ at magagamit ito para itama ang lahat ng ibang coupling. May dalawang natural na paraan para dito, na tinatawag na low-entanglement calibration (LEC):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**LEC on the IPR.** Rescale the excess of the IPR over its value for a uniform distribution, $2^{-n_A}$, by one factor per marginal:\n"
msgstr "**LEC sa IPR.** I-rescale ang sobra ng IPR kumpara sa halaga nito para sa uniform na distribution, $2^{-n_A}$, gamit ang isang factor kada marginal:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{LEC}}_A(J) = 2^{-n_A} + R_0\\bigl(\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{raw}}_A(J) - 2^{-n_A}\\bigr), \\qquad R_0 = \\frac{\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{ideal}}_A(J_0) - 2^{-n_A}}{\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{raw}}_A(J_0) - 2^{-n_A}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{LEC}}_A(J) = 2^{-n_A} + R_0\\bigl(\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{raw}}_A(J) - 2^{-n_A}\\bigr), \\qquad R_0 = \\frac{\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{ideal}}_A(J_0) - 2^{-n_A}}{\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{raw}}_A(J_0) - 2^{-n_A}}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**LEC on the $\\langle Z \\rangle$ expectation values.** Rescale every parity of the marginal by its own factor, and rebuild the IPR with the Parseval formula:\n"
msgstr "**LEC sa mga expectation value ng $\\langle Z \\rangle$.** I-rescale ang bawat parity ng marginal gamit ang sarili nitong factor, at buuin muli ang IPR gamit ang Parseval formula:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"r_S = \\frac{\\langle Z_S \\rangle^{\\mathrm{ideal}}(J_0)}{\\langle Z_S \\rangle^{\\mathrm{raw}}(J_0)}, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{LEC}}_A(J) = 2^{-n_A}\\Bigl(1 + \\sum_{S} r_S^2 \\, \\langle Z_S \\rangle^{\\mathrm{raw}}(J)^2\\Bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"r_S = \\frac{\\langle Z_S \\rangle^{\\mathrm{ideal}}(J_0)}{\\langle Z_S \\rangle^{\\mathrm{raw}}(J_0)}, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{LEC}}_A(J) = 2^{-n_A}\\Bigl(1 + \\sum_{S} r_S^2 \\, \\langle Z_S \\rangle^{\\mathrm{raw}}(J)^2\\Bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the code, each squared rescaled parity is debiased by subtracting its variance, as in section 2.\n"
msgstr "Sa code, ang bawat squared na rescaled parity ay dine-debias sa pamamagitan ng pagbabawas ng variance nito, tulad ng sa seksyon 2.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both are the same if every $r_S^2$ equals $R_0$.\n"
msgstr "Pareho lang ang dalawa kung ang bawat $r_S^2$ ay katumbas ng $R_0$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"> **Question.** What are the pros and cons of these methods?\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Pros**\n"
msgstr "**Pros**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Cheap:** no extra data is needed from the device, only a classical simulation at $J_0$.\n"
msgstr "**Mura:** walang karagdagang data na kailangan mula sa device, classical simulation lang sa $J_0$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Uses the structure of the circuit:** the circuit depth and the CZ layers do not change with $J$, so the noise at $J_0$ is the same noise as at every other $J$.\n"
msgstr "**Ginagamit ang istruktura ng circuit:** hindi nagbabago sa $J$ ang lalim ng circuit at ang mga CZ layer, kaya ang noise sa $J_0$ ay kapareho ng noise sa bawat ibang $J$.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Cons**\n"
msgstr "**Cons**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Assumes the effect of the noise on the observables does not depend on $J$:** the noise itself is the same, but how it damps the IPR or each $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ can change as $J$ grows.\n"
msgstr "**Ipinapalagay na hindi nakadepende sa $J$ ang epekto ng noise sa mga observable:** pareho ang noise mismo, pero maaaring magbago ang paraan ng pagpapahina nito sa IPR o sa bawat $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ habang lumalaki ang $J$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both methods on the noisy simulation {#both-methods-on-the-noisy-simulation}"
msgstr "Parehong paraan sa noisy na simulation {#both-methods-on-the-noisy-simulation}"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/onset-of-ergodicity/extracted-outputs/212cb53d-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/onset-of-ergodicity/extracted-outputs/212cb53d-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both methods remove most of the damage: the raw estimates in the previous plot are far too random, and the mitigated ones follow the exact curves. The differences show up for the larger marginals.\n"
msgstr "Inaalis ng parehong paraan ang karamihan sa pinsala: masyadong random ang mga raw na estimate sa nakaraang plot, at sinusundan ng mga na-mitigate ang mga eksaktong curve. Lumalabas ang mga pagkakaiba sa mas malalaking marginal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the small marginals both methods work. For the $3 \\times 3$ marginal, LEC on $\\langle Z \\rangle$ is clearly closer.\n"
msgstr "Sa maliliit na marginal, gumagana ang parehong paraan. Para sa $3 \\times 3$ na marginal, mas malapit nang malinaw ang LEC sa $\\langle Z \\rangle$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Why LEC on the IPR gives too little entropy.** Too little entropy means the IPR is too big: LEC on the IPR over-inflates it. It assumes that noise damps the contribution of every $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ to the IPR by the same factor. At $J_0$, every $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ is close to $\\pm 1$, so all strings contribute equally, and most strings have medium weight: of the 511 strings of a $3 \\times 3$ marginal, 252 have weight 4 or 5, and only nine have weight 1. Noise damps a string more the higher its weight (readout error alone damps a weight-$w$ string by $0.94^w$), so the single factor $R_0$ is set mainly by the damping of medium-weight strings. As $J$ grows, the higher-weight $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ decay fastest, and the IPR is carried more and more by low-weight strings, which noise damps less. Boosting them with a factor learned mainly from more heavily damped strings over-inflates the IPR. The effect grows with the size of the marginal, since a larger marginal has a wider range of weights. It is largest at intermediate $J$, after the mix of strings has shifted but while the excess of the IPR over its uniform value still matters.\n"
msgstr "**Bakit kulang ang entropy sa LEC sa IPR.** Ang kulang na entropy ay nangangahulugang masyadong malaki ang IPR: pinalalaki ito nang sobra ng LEC sa IPR. Ipinapalagay nito na pinapahina ng noise ang kontribusyon ng bawat $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ sa IPR gamit ang parehong factor. Sa $J_0$, malapit sa $\\pm 1$ ang bawat $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$, kaya pantay ang kontribusyon ng lahat ng string, at karamihan sa mga string ay may katamtamang weight: sa 511 string ng isang $3 \\times 3$ na marginal, 252 ang may weight na 4 o 5, at siyam lang ang may weight na 1. Mas pinapahina ng noise ang isang string kapag mas mataas ang weight nito (ang readout error lang ay pinapahina na ang isang string na may weight na $w$ ng $0.94^w$), kaya ang nag-iisang factor na $R_0$ ay pangunahing itinakda ng pagpapahina sa mga string na katamtaman ang weight. Habang lumalaki ang $J$, pinakamabilis na nawawala ang mga $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ na mas mataas ang weight, at ang IPR ay lalong dinadala ng mga string na mababa ang weight, na mas kaunti ang pagpapahina ng noise. Ang pagpapalakas sa mga ito gamit ang factor na pangunahing natutunan mula sa mas pinahinang mga string ay sobrang nagpapalaki sa IPR. Lumalaki ang epektong ito kasabay ng laki ng marginal, dahil mas malawak ang saklaw ng weight ng mas malaking marginal. Pinakamalaki ito sa katamtamang $J$, pagkatapos lumipat ang halo ng mga string pero mahalaga pa rin ang sobra ng IPR sa uniform na halaga nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Why LEC on $\\langle Z \\rangle$ errs the other way.** It rescales each string by its own factor, so the shift between weights does not affect it. It only assumes that each string keeps its $J_0$ damping. As $J$ grows, each $Z_S$ spreads into higher-weight operators, which pick up more noise than at $J_0$, so the factors slightly under-correct and the entropy comes out slightly too high.\n"
msgstr "**Bakit kabaligtaran ang mali ng LEC sa $\\langle Z \\rangle$.** Nire-rescale nito ang bawat string gamit ang sarili nitong factor, kaya hindi ito apektado ng paglipat sa pagitan ng mga weight. Ipinapalagay lang nito na napapanatili ng bawat string ang pagpapahina nito sa $J_0$. Habang lumalaki ang $J$, kumakalat ang bawat $Z_S$ sa mga operator na mas mataas ang weight, na mas maraming noise ang nakukuha kaysa sa $J_0$, kaya bahagyang kulang ang pagtatama ng mga factor at bahagyang masyadong mataas ang lumalabas na entropy.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "So the prediction to test on hardware is: **the larger the marginal, the more LEC on $\\langle Z \\rangle$ should win**. On hardware, the noise is stronger and not of a known form.\n"
msgstr "Kaya ang prediksyon na susubukan sa hardware ay: **habang mas malaki ang marginal, mas dapat manalo ang LEC sa $\\langle Z \\rangle$**. Sa hardware, mas malakas ang noise at hindi ito kilalang anyo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Run at scale {#4-run-at-scale}"
msgstr "4. Patakbuhin nang malakihan {#4-run-at-scale}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The hardware experiment runs an $8 \\times 8$ lattice with four cycles: 64 qubits and 1,344 CZ gates in 48 layers, at nine couplings. Five things change compared with the simulation:\n"
msgstr "Ang hardware experiment ay nagpapatakbo ng $8 \\times 8$ na lattice na may apat na cycle: 64 qubit at 1,344 CZ gate sa 48 layer, sa siyam na coupling. Limang bagay ang nagbabago kumpara sa simulation:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The noise has to be **learned**, which only works if the CZ layers are fixed.\n"
msgstr "Kailangang **matutunan** ang noise, na gumagana lang kung nakapirmi ang mga CZ layer.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Twirling** turns the noise of each layer into a Pauli channel, which can be learned and amplified.\n"
msgstr "Ginagawa ng **Twirling** na Pauli channel ang noise ng bawat layer, na maaaring matutunan at palakasin.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Dynamical decoupling (DD)** protects idle qubits.\n"
msgstr "Pinoprotektahan ng **Dynamical decoupling (DD)** ang mga idle na qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Noise amplification** for PEA runs in the same job as the main data.\n"
msgstr "Ang **Noise amplification** para sa PEA ay tumatakbo sa parehong job ng pangunahing data.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**MPS simulations** at small $J$ provide the classical references for LEC-based error mitigation.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga **MPS simulation** sa maliit na $J$ ang nagbibigay ng mga classical na reference para sa error mitigation na nakabatay sa LEC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The cells that need a backend only run when `RUN_ON_HARDWARE` is `True`. MPS simulations can be rerun with `COMPUTE_MPS_REFERENCES` set to `True`. The other cells run here.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga cell na nangangailangan ng backend ay tumatakbo lang kapag ang `RUN_ON_HARDWARE` ay `True`. Maaaring patakbuhin muli ang mga MPS simulation kapag ang `COMPUTE_MPS_REFERENCES` ay nakatakda sa `True`. Ang iba pang mga cell ay tumatakbo dito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fixed CZ layers {#fixed-cz-layers}"
msgstr "Mga nakapirming CZ layer {#fixed-cz-layers}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Boxes for noise learning {#boxes-for-noise-learning}"
msgstr "Mga box para sa noise learning {#boxes-for-noise-learning}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Samplomatic boxing pass manager then groups each circuit into *boxes*: one per CZ layer and one for the measurements. Each box carries a reference to the noise model it needs, so you can check that all couplings share the same boxes. The next cell does this for the $8 \\times 8$ circuits of the hardware run, compiled to CZ gates without a backend, and prints the boxes that noise learning will characterize.\n"
msgstr "Pagkatapos, ang Samplomatic boxing pass manager ay naghahati ng bawat circuit sa mga *box*: isa para sa bawat CZ layer at isa para sa mga measurement. May dalang reference ang bawat box sa noise model na kailangan nito, kaya masusuri mo kung pareho ang mga box ng lahat ng coupling. Ginagawa ito ng susunod na cell para sa mga $8 \\times 8$ na circuit ng hardware run, na na-compile sa mga CZ gate nang walang backend, at inililimbag ang mga box na iku-characterize ng noise learning.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Twirl the circuits {#twirl-the-circuits}"
msgstr "I-twirl ang mga circuit {#twirl-the-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In every randomization, Samplomatic puts random Pauli gates before each box and the compensating gates after it, merged into the neighboring single-qubit gates. Averaged over randomizations, the noise of each layer becomes a Pauli channel, which `NoiseLearnerV3` can learn as a sparse Pauli-Lindblad model and the PEA step can amplify. Measurement twirling randomly flips bits before readout. The flips are undone in software, which makes the readout noise symmetric and is the basis of the readout correction (TREX).\n"
msgstr "Sa bawat randomization, naglalagay ang Samplomatic ng mga random na Pauli gate bago ang bawat box at ng mga compensating na gate pagkatapos nito, na isinama sa mga katabing single-qubit gate. Kapag inaverage sa mga randomization, nagiging Pauli channel ang noise ng bawat layer, na maaaring matutunan ng `NoiseLearnerV3` bilang sparse Pauli-Lindblad model at mapalakas ng hakbang ng PEA. Ang measurement twirling ay random na bumabaligtad ng mga bit bago ang readout. Binabawi ang mga pagbaligtad na ito sa software, na ginagawang simetriko ang readout noise at siyang batayan ng readout correction (TREX).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The hardware workflow {#the-hardware-workflow}"
msgstr "Ang hardware workflow {#the-hardware-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose the qubits, compile the circuits, then learn the noise and run the sweep. These cells are switched off here.\n"
msgstr "Piliin ang mga qubit, i-compile ang mga circuit, pagkatapos ay alamin ang noise at patakbuhin ang sweep. Naka-off ang mga cell na ito rito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Choose the qubits.** Nighthawk's square grid holds the $8 \\times 8$ lattice without SWAP gates. The cell scores every $8 \\times 8$ rectangle of the grid by its reported CZ and readout errors and takes the best.\n"
msgstr "**Piliin ang mga qubit.** Kasya sa square grid ng Nighthawk ang $8 \\times 8$ na lattice nang walang SWAP gate. Binibigyan ng cell ng score ang bawat $8 \\times 8$ na parihaba ng grid ayon sa iniulat nitong CZ at readout error at kinukuha ang pinakamahusay.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Compile.** The same steps as above on the chosen qubits, followed by `build`, which turns each boxed circuit into a template circuit and a *samplex*, the recipe for drawing the twirling gates and the injected noise. DD is added to the templates.\n"
msgstr "**I-compile.** Parehong mga hakbang tulad ng nasa itaas sa mga napiling qubit, na sinusundan ng `build`, na ginagawang template circuit at isang *samplex* ang bawat boxed na circuit, ang recipe para sa pagguhit ng mga twirling gate at ng ini-inject na noise. Idinadagdag ang DD sa mga template.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Learn the noise and run the sweep.** One `NoiseLearnerV3` job learns all five boxes: a Pauli-Lindblad model for each of the four CZ layers, and the readout noise of the measurement box. Then one `QuantumProgram` holds all nine couplings. Each item gets its template, its samplex, the learned noise models, and three noise scales. A scale of 0 is the unamplified data for both LEC methods. Scales of 0.5 and 1 add 50% and 100% of the learned noise for PEA, which extrapolates back to zero noise. This uses about 40 seconds of QPU time.\n"
msgstr "**Alamin ang noise at patakbuhin ang sweep.** Isang `NoiseLearnerV3` job ang natututo sa lahat ng limang box: isang Pauli-Lindblad model para sa bawat isa sa apat na CZ layer, at ang readout noise ng measurement box. Pagkatapos, hawak ng isang `QuantumProgram` ang lahat ng siyam na coupling. Nakakakuha ang bawat item ng template nito, samplex nito, mga natutunang noise model, at tatlong noise scale. Ang scale na 0 ay ang hindi pinalakas na data para sa parehong LEC method. Ang mga scale na 0.5 at 1 ay nagdadagdag ng 50% at 100% ng natutunang noise para sa PEA, na nag-e-extrapolate pabalik sa zero na noise. Gumagamit ito ng mga 40 segundo ng QPU time.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. The hardware data {#5-the-hardware-data}"
msgstr "5. Ang hardware data {#5-the-hardware-data}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This section explores how the previous methods perform on real hardware data from a Nighthawk processor.\n"
msgstr "Sinusuri ng seksyong ito kung paano gumagana ang mga naunang paraan sa totoong hardware data mula sa isang Nighthawk processor.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Load the run {#load-the-run}"
msgstr "I-load ang run {#load-the-run}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With `RUN_ON_HARDWARE` set to `True`, the next cell converts the results of the two jobs from section 4 and saves them to `data/hardware_run_new.npz`, in the same format as the saved run, so the new run can be analyzed again later. Otherwise it loads the saved run from `data/hardware_run.npz`. The bits are packed along the qubit axis to save space.\n"
msgstr "Kapag ang `RUN_ON_HARDWARE` ay nakatakda sa `True`, kino-convert ng susunod na cell ang mga resulta ng dalawang job mula sa seksyon 4 at sine-save ang mga ito sa `data/hardware_run_new.npz`, sa parehong format ng naka-save na run, para maanalisa muli ang bagong run sa ibang pagkakataon. Kung hindi, nilo-load nito ang naka-save na run mula sa `data/hardware_run.npz`. Ang mga bit ay naka-pack sa kahabaan ng qubit axis para makatipid ng espasyo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the kernel restarts while the jobs run, do not submit them again. Rerun the cells before the last call in section 4, check that the same qubits are chosen, and set `learner_job` and `executor_job` to `service.job(job_id)` with the job IDs that were printed out in section 4.\n"
msgstr "Kung mag-restart ang kernel habang tumatakbo ang mga job, huwag silang isumite muli. Patakbuhin muli ang mga cell bago ang huling tawag sa seksyon 4, tiyaking pareho ang mga napiling qubit, at itakda ang `learner_job` at `executor_job` sa `service.job(job_id)` gamit ang mga job ID na inilimbag sa seksyon 4.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Classical references {#classical-references}"
msgstr "Mga classical na reference {#classical-references}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both LEC methods need the ideal marginal distributions at $J_0 = 0.005\\pi$, and testing them needs ideal values at the held-out couplings $J = 0.01\\pi$ and $0.02\\pi$. These come from matrix product state (MPS) simulations, saved for every placement of each marginal shape on the lattice, as in the paper, and for every non-overlapping $2 \\times 2$ block at $J_0$. At $J_0$ they converge at bond dimension $\\chi = 64$. At $J = 0.01\\pi$ and $0.02\\pi$ they use $\\chi = 128$, and at $0.02\\pi$ they still change by up to about 13% from $\\chi = 64$ for $3 \\times 3$ marginals, so treat them as approximate there. The next cell computes them if `COMPUTE_MPS_REFERENCES` is `True`, which takes about 18 minutes, and otherwise loads the saved results, keyed by coupling index, bond dimension, and marginal.\n"
msgstr "Kailangan ng parehong LEC method ang mga ideal na marginal distribution sa $J_0 = 0.005\\pi$, at ang pagsubok sa mga ito ay nangangailangan ng mga ideal na halaga sa mga held-out na coupling na $J = 0.01\\pi$ at $0.02\\pi$. Galing ang mga ito sa mga matrix product state (MPS) simulation, na naka-save para sa bawat placement ng bawat hugis ng marginal sa lattice, tulad sa paper, at para sa bawat hindi nag-o-overlap na $2 \\times 2$ na block sa $J_0$. Sa $J_0$, nagko-converge ang mga ito sa bond dimension na $\\chi = 64$. Sa $J = 0.01\\pi$ at $0.02\\pi$, gumagamit sila ng $\\chi = 128$, at sa $0.02\\pi$ nagbabago pa rin sila nang hanggang mga 13% mula sa $\\chi = 64$ para sa mga $3 \\times 3$ na marginal, kaya ituring silang tinatayang halaga roon. Kinakalkula ang mga ito ng susunod na cell kung ang `COMPUTE_MPS_REFERENCES` ay `True`, na tumatagal nang mga 18 minuto, at kung hindi, nilo-load nito ang mga naka-save na resulta, na naka-key ayon sa coupling index, bond dimension, at marginal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Data quality: faulty couplers / qubits {#data-quality-faulty-couplers--qubits}"
msgstr "Kalidad ng data: mga may sira na coupler / qubit {#data-quality-faulty-couplers--qubits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, look at the lowest coupling, $J_0$, where the expectation values should be close to the Néel checkerboard.\n"
msgstr "Una, tingnan ang pinakamababang coupling, $J_0$, kung saan dapat malapit sa Néel checkerboard ang mga expectation value.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/onset-of-ergodicity/extracted-outputs/48d2dbbb-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/onset-of-ergodicity/extracted-outputs/48d2dbbb-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "> **Question.** Looking at the hardware map, what stands out?\n"
msgstr "> **Tanong.** Kapag tiningnan ang hardware map, ano ang kapansin-pansin?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The pale sites, which have lost almost all of their signal although the state at $J_0$ is close to the Néel state. They matter because LEC divides by whatever signal survives at $J_0$: a qubit with almost no signal gives a huge, noisy correction factor, and a few such qubits can dominate every marginal that contains them.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga maputlang site, na halos nawala ang lahat ng signal kahit malapit sa Néel state ang state sa $J_0$. Mahalaga ang mga ito dahil hinahati ng LEC sa anumang signal na natitira sa $J_0$: ang qubit na halos walang signal ay nagbibigay ng napakalaki at maingay na correction factor, at ilang ganitong qubit ay maaaring mangibabaw sa bawat marginal na may kasamang mga ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A rule that uses only the data: A qubit is faulty if its single-qubit IPR at $J_0$ is within $0.25^2/2 \\approx 0.03$ of $1/2$, the value for a fully mixed qubit. Since the IPR of one qubit is $(1 + \\langle Z \\rangle^2)/2$, this flags qubits with $|\\langle Z \\rangle| < 0.25$. Marginals that contain a flagged site are left out below.\n"
msgstr "Isang panuntunang data lang ang ginagamit: may sira ang isang qubit kung ang single-qubit IPR nito sa $J_0$ ay nasa loob ng $0.25^2/2 \\approx 0.03$ mula sa $1/2$, ang halaga para sa isang ganap na mixed na qubit. Dahil ang IPR ng isang qubit ay $(1 + \\langle Z \\rangle^2)/2$, tinutukoy nito ang mga qubit na may $|\\langle Z \\rangle| < 0.25$. Hindi isinasama sa ibaba ang mga marginal na may kasamang naka-flag na site.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Select the marginals to average {#select-the-marginals-to-average}"
msgstr "Piliin ang mga marginal na i-aaverage {#select-the-marginals-to-average}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The next cell shows which placements of each shape enter the averages below: every placement in the bulk of the lattice without a flagged site (red crosses). Placements that touch the edge (shaded) are left out. Edge qubits have fewer bonds, so they scramble more slowly. Averaged on their own, they cross over a full step of $J$ later than bulk placements, for every shape and method. Each averaged placement has its own box, colored by placement.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng susunod na cell kung aling mga placement ng bawat hugis ang pumapasok sa mga average sa ibaba: bawat placement sa bulk ng lattice na walang naka-flag na site (mga pulang krus). Hindi isinasama ang mga placement na dumidikit sa gilid (may shade). Mas kaunti ang bond ng mga edge qubit, kaya mas mabagal silang nag-scramble. Kapag inaverage nang mag-isa, nagko-crossover sila nang isang buong hakbang ng $J$ mamaya kaysa sa mga bulk placement, para sa bawat hugis at paraan. May sariling box ang bawat in-average na placement, na may kulay ayon sa placement.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/onset-of-ergodicity/extracted-outputs/d31b217b-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/onset-of-ergodicity/extracted-outputs/d31b217b-0.avif)\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEA {#pea}"
msgstr "PEA {#pea}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The third method needs no classical reference. For each parity, take the values at noise factors 1, 1.5, and 2, divide out the learned readout damping (TREX), fit an exponential in the noise factor, and extrapolate to zero noise. Parities that change sign or are nearly zero get a straight-line fit. Subtracting the variance needs a reliable estimate of it, which is easy for raw and rescaled parities but not for the output of a nonlinear fit with clipping and fallbacks. PEA therefore uses the other standard way to remove the bias of a square. Extrapolate each half of the randomizations separately and multiply the two independent estimates.\n"
msgstr "Hindi na kailangan ng classical na reference ang ikatlong paraan. Para sa bawat parity, kunin ang mga halaga sa noise factor na 1, 1.5, at 2, hatiin sa natutunang readout damping (TREX), mag-fit ng exponential sa noise factor, at mag-extrapolate sa zero na noise. Ang mga parity na nagpapalit ng sign o halos zero ay nakakakuha ng straight-line fit. Ang pagbabawas ng variance ay nangangailangan ng maaasahang estimate nito, na madali para sa raw at rescaled na mga parity pero hindi para sa output ng nonlinear na fit na may clipping at mga fallback. Kaya gumagamit ang PEA ng isa pang karaniwang paraan para alisin ang bias ng isang square. I-extrapolate nang hiwalay ang bawat kalahati ng mga randomization at i-multiply ang dalawang independent na estimate.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "All four estimates, and the crossovers {#all-four-estimates-and-the-crossovers}"
msgstr "Lahat ng apat na estimate, at ang mga crossover {#all-four-estimates-and-the-crossovers}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The next function computes the raw, LEC-on-IPR, LEC-on-$\\langle Z \\rangle$, and PEA estimates of the IPR of one marginal position at every coupling. It also estimates the shot noise of each, by bootstrapping the randomizations. The cell runs it for every placement that enters the averages, which takes about a minute and a half.\n"
msgstr "Kinakalkula ng susunod na function ang raw, LEC-on-IPR, LEC-on-$\\langle Z \\rangle$, at PEA na mga estimate ng IPR ng isang posisyon ng marginal sa bawat coupling. Tinatantya rin nito ang shot noise ng bawat isa, sa pamamagitan ng pag-bootstrap sa mga randomization. Pinapatakbo ito ng cell para sa bawat placement na pumapasok sa mga average, na tumatagal nang mga isa't kalahating minuto.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/onset-of-ergodicity/extracted-outputs/6303dec9-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/onset-of-ergodicity/extracted-outputs/6303dec9-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Wrap-up {#wrap-up}"
msgstr "Pagbubuod {#wrap-up}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "What it took to run an experiment of this size:\n"
msgstr "Ang kinailangan para magpatakbo ng experiment na ganito kalaki:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Circuits whose structure does not depend on $J$**, compiled one sublayer at a time, so one noise model serves the whole sweep.\n"
msgstr "**Mga circuit na ang istruktura ay hindi nakadepende sa $J$**, na na-compile nang isang sublayer sa bawat pagkakataon, kaya isang noise model ang nagsisilbi sa buong sweep.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Estimators that work from bitstrings**: pair counting for the IPR of a marginal, and the Parseval form, with the variance subtracted from each squared parity, when the inputs are mitigated expectation values.\n"
msgstr "**Mga estimator na gumagana mula sa mga bitstring**: pair counting para sa IPR ng isang marginal, at ang Parseval form, na binabawasan ng variance ang bawat squared na parity, kapag mga na-mitigate na expectation value ang input.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**A cheap classical anchor**: the ideal state at small $J$ calibrates the noise, and held-out couplings test the calibration. Calibrating each $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ separately, rather than the IPR as a whole, is what makes the large marginals agree.\n"
msgstr "**Isang murang classical na angkla**: ang ideal na state sa maliit na $J$ ang nagka-calibrate ng noise, at sinusubok ng mga held-out na coupling ang calibration. Ang hiwalay na pag-calibrate sa bawat $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$, sa halip na sa IPR sa kabuuan, ang dahilan kung bakit nagkakasundo ang malalaking marginal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**IBM tools for the heavy lifting**: Samplomatic boxes and twirling, `NoiseLearnerV3`, dynamical decoupling, and one `Executor` job with noise amplification for PEA.\n"
msgstr "**Mga tool ng IBM para sa mabibigat na gawain**: mga Samplomatic box at twirling, `NoiseLearnerV3`, dynamical decoupling, at isang `Executor` job na may noise amplification para sa PEA.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Data-quality checks** that use only the data.\n"
msgstr "**Mga pagsusuri sa kalidad ng data** na data lang ang ginagamit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Next steps.** To go further with mitigation, see the [probabilistic error amplification](/tutorials/probabilistic-error-amplification) and [PEC with shaded lightcones](/tutorials/pec-with-shaded-lightcones) tutorials.\n"
msgstr "**Mga susunod na hakbang.** Para lumalim pa sa mitigation, tingnan ang mga tutorial na [probabilistic error amplification](/tutorials/probabilistic-error-amplification) at [PEC with shaded lightcones](/tutorials/pec-with-shaded-lightcones).\n"

